menu "AlgaOps current sensor (optional, clamp-on CT)"

    config ALGAOPS_CURRENT_ENABLE
        bool "A clamp-on current transformer is connected"
        default n
        help
            Optional motor-current channel.  Use only a split-core current
            transformer with a built-in burden and voltage output (for example
            0-1 V AC at rated current), clamped around ONE insulated conductor
            through a commercial AC line splitter or installed by a qualified
            electrician.  Never open a live enclosure or strip insulation.
            The CT output is biased to mid-supply and read on an ADC1 pin.
            Without a CT the node publishes no "current_a" and the gateway
            infers the operating mode from vibration.

    config ALGAOPS_CURRENT_ADC_GPIO
        int "ADC1 GPIO of the CT signal"
        depends on ALGAOPS_CURRENT_ENABLE
        range 32 39
        default 34
        help
            ESP32 ADC1 pins only (GPIO 32-39); ADC2 is unavailable while
            Wi-Fi is running.

    config ALGAOPS_CURRENT_MA_PER_VOLT
        int "CT scale: milliamps per volt RMS of the CT output"
        depends on ALGAOPS_CURRENT_ENABLE
        range 100 1000000
        default 30000
        help
            Rated primary current divided by the rated output voltage, for
            example 30 A / 1 V = 30000 mA/V.  Check the transformer label and
            calibrate against a reference clamp meter on the real pump.

    config ALGAOPS_CURRENT_SAMPLE_HZ
        int "ADC sampling rate (Hz)"
        depends on ALGAOPS_CURRENT_ENABLE
        range 500 1000
        default 1000
        help
            Samples are taken by a dedicated task with a 1 ms FreeRTOS tick
            (CONFIG_FREERTOS_HZ=1000): 20 samples per 50 Hz mains cycle.

endmenu
